ose two  Stallone insisted on practical gags I  mean that in and of itself the the  amount we did in the time we did it in  practical gags with squibs and fire was  it makes my hands Shake today it makes  my palms sweaty because every day  something epic could go wrong and you  had to have your [ __ ] together you  couldn't just say well fix it in post  We'll erase the wire like we're out in  the middle of Thailand and you had to  get it right and that was you know you  know 11 stunt teams from all over the  world doing that was impressive the  other thing on the other spectrum of the  scale this is a little known movie that  I probably wasn't received all that well  I I went in and did a bunch of work on  After Earth for M night shyaman there  was one little sequence where Jaden  Smith has to jump off the cliff and the  final picture they did a ton of digital  work and it looks like it was against  blue screen but for two weeks me and one  of the best aerial coordinators in the  business a guy named Tim Rigby far the  best wingsuit guys on the planet went to  the Swiss Alps and off the Iger we did  14 000 foot wingsuit jumps they call it  proximity flying where every jump you  know really bad things can happen for  the cameraman who has to fly with a a 45  pound camera on his head so you can  imagine what that is as he's literally  just a few meters Off the Wall going at  terminal velocity following another guy  weaving the thing to this day it is the  most I even get choked up thinking about  it it's the most hair raising most  you're on the ground just going please  don't die please don't like you've heard  the best in the world but once they  leave that helicopter at 14 000 feet  they come into about 12 000 feet where  they have to link up against the Iger  and go down and follow each other  through some of the most insane weather  conditions that the Swiss Alps can offer  when you finally see those two  parachutes open  there is no describing the amount of  relief for like  it's like it still gets me going today  and we did that over the course of two  weeks I remember the day when you know  you're checking off your shot list and  we finally get footage and then you're  just well it's still nice weather we can  go back and you just know no we're done  we're done and that was the biggest  relief I've ever felt in my career that  we got amazing footage whether it made  the final product or not and uh push I  think we pushed the limits of what at  least in that endeavor human beings  could do we walked away without a  scratch and that is one of my proudest  moments so I'd go with those two both  great stories and uh yeah I could never  I could never do these things just never  never I don't know if I do them again  I'm glad I did them but I'm good we  rolled the dice and we pushed and the  universe didn't push back so we're good
 

